WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.500
After delivering a stunning finale to&nbsp;
Marvel's "Guardians of the Galaxy" trilogy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:09.420
James Gunn has proven that he knows how to handle&nbsp;
cosmic heroes with complex emotions. And that’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:13.020
exactly what Superman needs right now.
Some spoilers for Guardians&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:15.240
of the Galaxy Vol. 3 ahead.
Is Gunn really right for Superman?&nbsp;

00:00:15.431 --> 00:00:19.691
James Gunn’s appointment as the head of&nbsp;
DC’s cinematic universe seemed logical.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.691 --> 00:00:23.460
The director had made some of Marvel’s best&nbsp;
films with the “Guardians of the Galaxy” series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:28.140
and he delivered the most acclaimed DC movie&nbsp;
in years, “The Suicide Squad,” in 2021.&nbsp;

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:33.069
But you might wonder why Gunn would choose to&nbsp;
write and direct a new Superman movie himself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.069 --> 00:00:37.860
The character has been hard to adapt for the&nbsp;
big screen in the modern era, and Henry Cavill’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:43.620
version, though popular with some fans, didn’t&nbsp;
last. Gunn also has a knack for witty sarcasm that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:48.480
suits “Guardians of the Galaxy,” but might clash&nbsp;
with the Man of Steel. So the question remains: Is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:51.000
Gunn the right choice to direct a Superman movie?

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:52.372
"That's a good question." 

00:00:52.372 --> 00:00:57.420
After watching “Guardians of the Galaxy Vol.&nbsp;
3,” the answer is a clear yes. Though the two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:02.820
franchises differ in style and tone, “Vol. 3”&nbsp;
shows how good Gunn is at the things that count:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:08.040
character development, emotional resonance,&nbsp;
and heart. Amidst all the humor and colorful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:12.540
alien settings, the movie returns to what&nbsp;
made the MCU great, honoring both its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:17.220
heroes and the time fans have spent with them.
In short, “Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3” has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:20.340
sold us on James Gunn’s “Superman: Legacy” movie.
What Superman is all about&nbsp;

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:24.780
Superman’s bright outfit, catchy name, and&nbsp;
dedication to helping those in need set the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:29.220
standard for everything that followed, including&nbsp;
the modern comic book blockbuster industry.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:33.960
But the world of caped comic characters has&nbsp;
changed a lot since then. It’s not enough to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:39.178
just save people anymore – you need over-the-top&nbsp;
enemies, a multiverse, and countless crossovers.&nbsp;

00:01:39.178 --> 00:01:43.020
Maybe it’s the simplicity of his&nbsp;
costume or his Swiss army knife powers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:47.940
but Superman has managed to stay above the noise,&nbsp;
and still represents the spirit of those golden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:53.640
days. Clark Kent is known for being good, and&nbsp;
kind, and brave, and true, even in the darkest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:58.334
of times. He does the right thing, which is&nbsp;
why we love superheroes in the first place.&nbsp;

00:01:58.334 --> 00:02:03.000
"Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3" understands&nbsp;
that message. It’s accurate in its portrayal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:07.080
of what makes its heroes heroic. In the&nbsp;
film’s final act, the team fights through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:11.820
a whole ship of bad guys; not to kill the&nbsp;
main villain or find the last Infinity Stone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:17.400
but to save the many innocents trapped there.
Kids, aliens, baby animals – every single life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:22.860
matters, and they all get out alive. After nearly&nbsp;
a decade of action-packed climaxes and battles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:28.320
against Thanos and his ilk, the Guardians end&nbsp;
their trilogy by saving lives, not doing stunts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.401 --> 00:02:31.281
And that’s what Superman is all about.
Characters, not cameos

00:02:31.281 --> 00:02:36.780
Marvel Studios has had plenty of hits since the&nbsp;
Infinity Saga ended, including "Loki", "Black&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:45.120
Panther: Wakanda Forever," and "WandaVision."
"What is grief, if not love persevering?"

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:48.840
But there have also been more&nbsp;
than a few duds. At its worst,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:52.740
the franchise has become a focus-tested&nbsp;
mishmash of setups, Easter eggs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:57.360
and "spot the cameo" moments. Fortunately,&nbsp;
"Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3" is the good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:02.400
kind of Marvel movie -- one that focuses on real&nbsp;
character development instead of cheap callbacks.&nbsp;

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:07.320
"Vol. 3" cashes in on nine years of buildup.&nbsp;
We get to see Nebula become an inspiring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:12.660
leader after a tragic, rage-filled life. Rocket&nbsp;
overcomes his immense trauma and finally accepts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:17.708
himself as he is. These arcs work because of how&nbsp;
much time we've all spent with the characters.&nbsp;

00:03:17.708 --> 00:03:22.560
Though he's a larger-than-life figure, Superman&nbsp;
needs that same kind of attention. The character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:27.960
fails when he's treated as less than a person and&nbsp;
more than a god -- a titanic emblem of goodness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:33.480
with no actual arc to speak of. The appeal&nbsp;
of Kal-El is that he chooses to be Superman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:37.800
time after time, even though he could just&nbsp;
as easily conquer all of Earth in an instant.&nbsp;

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:42.960
Additionally, Superman needs to stand on his&nbsp;
own, apart from any other sub-series or Justice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:48.120
League teammates. If he is to be the heart of&nbsp;
Gunn's new DCU, it needs to be a heart that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:51.360
beats and bleeds, and not just a logo.
The emotional core of "Guardians"

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:55.800
Though they're still silly more often than they're&nbsp;
not, the "Guardians of the Galaxy" films may also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.800 --> 00:04:01.140
be the most emotionally complex in all of the&nbsp;
MCU. Each one of the main characters is deeply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:05.760
flawed and haunted by the ghosts of their pasts.
Over the course of the story, they're all forced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:09.840
to confront their traumas, ultimately finding&nbsp;
new things to fight for and ways to improve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:14.580
themselves. "Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3"&nbsp;
continues with that trend, giving the team an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:16.406
emotionally resonant sendoff.

00:04:16.406 --> 00:04:18.240
"That is the gist of it." 

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:23.220
Gunn's ability to handle messy characters and&nbsp;
emotionally muddled storylines makes him a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:28.080
great choice for the DCU, and for Superman&nbsp;
in particular. Clark Kent might seem like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:33.240
a much more sunshine-and-rainbows character than&nbsp;
other DC heroes like Batman or John Constantine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:37.920
but telling his story the right way requires an&nbsp;
understanding of the complicated world around him.&nbsp;

00:04:38.141 --> 00:04:43.020
He too is a man born of tragedy, shipped away&nbsp;
from his family and his entire home planet while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:48.300
just a baby. Out of that tragedy, and with the&nbsp;
guidance of some compassionate adoptive parents,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:52.067
he discovers the drive to help the&nbsp;
helpless wherever they might be.&nbsp;

00:04:52.067 --> 00:04:56.760
Superman's strength is born of grief, just&nbsp;
like the Guardians of the Galaxy. Hopefully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.760 --> 00:05:00.480
Gunn's strong track record of writing&nbsp;
nuanced comic book character arcs will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:03.720
parlay into a fantastic Man of Steel film.
What "Superman: Legacy" could look like

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:07.740
Few details have been revealed about James&nbsp;
Gunn's Superman movie, which is set to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:12.960
released in 2025. However, the writer-director&nbsp;
has dropped a couple of clues. Speaking about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:17.468
the script on Twitter in March of 2023, Gunn&nbsp;
said that the story will largely focus on,&nbsp;

00:05:17.468 --> 00:05:22.740
"Superman's heritage - how both his aristocratic&nbsp;
Kryptonian parents and his Kansas farmer parents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:27.060
inform who he is and the choices he makes."
What exactly does that have to do with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:32.160
"Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3?" Well, a lot,&nbsp;
actually. Consider Rocket's arc in the third&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:37.200
"Guardians" film. He has to deal with a violent&nbsp;
and complicated history in order to become the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:42.240
hero he knows he can be. Sound familiar?
How about Nebula and Gamora, who both have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:47.040
to grapple with their dark upbringing by Thanos&nbsp;
in order to take ownership of their lives? For&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:51.720
his entire comic book movie career, Gunn has been&nbsp;
telling stories about how our history shapes us;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:55.380
about how it determines our paths, and&nbsp;
the ways we can break away from it.&nbsp;

00:05:55.634 --> 00:05:59.460
From the sound of it, Gunn's "Superman:&nbsp;
Legacy" will be as much about Krypton&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:03.060
as Earth. For a director who's built&nbsp;
his reputation on the backs of sci-fi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:07.500
superhero movies, that makes a lot of sense.
Of course, the two will still be quite different,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:12.000
with Gunn telling Rolling Stone in April 2023,
"It's not like Superman is going to have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:15.862
exactly the same vibe as a Guardians&nbsp;
movie. It's actually quite different."&nbsp;

00:06:15.862 --> 00:06:20.100
We still have a while to wait before Gunn's&nbsp;
Superman vision becomes clear, but "Guardians&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:24.060
of the Galaxy Vol. 3" is a strong endorsement&nbsp;
of what the director could be cooking up.

